WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.166
Behind every wind turbine and solar panel,

2
00:00:03.166 --> 00:00:06.332
there are digital controllers to keep operations running.

3
00:00:06.332 --> 00:00:08.970
When a device does something unexpected,

4
00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:11.609
how do you spot it—and know something is wrong?

5
00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:15.302
Many of these controllers are too limited to run conventional antivirus.

6
00:00:15.302 --> 00:00:16.885
Network monitoring helps—

7
00:00:16.885 --> 00:00:20.051
but LayerOne adds visibility into the controller’s physical activity.

8
00:00:20.051 --> 00:00:21.634
Meet LayerOne.

9
00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:24.800
A new perspective on device security.

10
00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.494
Watch the physical activity behind the software.

11
00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:31.132
As a controller executes tasks,

12
00:00:31.132 --> 00:00:33.771
it draws current through its power pins,

13
00:00:33.771 --> 00:00:35.882
creating electrical signatures.

14
00:00:35.882 --> 00:00:40.103
LayerOne measures these patterns to establish a normal baseline.

15
00:00:40.103 --> 00:00:43.797
Malware can introduce unexpected tasks that alter those patterns,

16
00:00:43.797 --> 00:00:46.435
allowing LayerOne to flag suspicious changes.

17
00:00:46.435 --> 00:00:49.601
It watches from outside the production network.

18
00:00:49.601 --> 00:00:51.712
No endpoint agent to disable.

19
00:00:51.712 --> 00:00:53.822
No IP address there to discover.

20
00:00:53.822 --> 00:00:56.988
Signed alerts travel over independent LoRa radio

21
00:00:56.988 --> 00:00:59.099
to central command.

22
00:00:59.099 --> 00:01:03.320
An additional layer of visibility, complementing your existing security.

23
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.431
Evidence stays in a separate record,

24
00:01:05.431 --> 00:01:09.125
ready to retrieve with a secure hardware key.

25
00:01:09.125 --> 00:01:10.708
LayerOne.

26
00:01:10.708 --> 00:01:11.974
See deeper.

27
00:01:11.974 --> 00:01:13.452
Know sooner.
